We don't believe in chance at Nimber.
## Caught your eye? Great. Keep going...
We are Nimber, and we are not just filling positions, we are building a team that is ready to shake things up. If you are ready to rewrite the rules and make a real impact, this is your moment. Join us and let's put the future where it belongs. In the hands of passionate people.
But what does Nimber mean?
In mathematics and game theory, they are numbers with special properties of addition and multiplication. And what we really want is to add value to customers' projects.
Position: DevOps Engineer
Location: Porto or Lisbon, Portugal
Work model: Remote
Join a team building and operating the cloud foundation for AI use cases, agents and data products, making them reliable, scalable and secure in production across an international organisation.
## Responsibilities
• Build and operate cloud-native infrastructure for AI solutions, data pipelines, APIs, agents and platform services, with Azure as the main platform and AWS where required;
• Create reusable infrastructure, deployment, observability and environment patterns to move AI use cases from prototype to production faster;
• Automate provisioning, configuration, CI/CD, monitoring, logging, secrets management and cost controls;
• Support cloud architecture decisions for agentic workflows, model integrations, event-driven services and data platforms;
• Work with security teams to ensure identity, access, encryption, logging and resilience standards are met;
• Collaborate with local IT teams to onboard environments, troubleshoot deployments and scale successful AI use cases;
• Continuously improve platform reliability, developer experience and cloud cost transparency.
## Requirements
• Experience with cloud-native development and deployment, ideally strong Azure and practical exposure to AWS;
• Infrastructure as Code (IaC), CI/CD, containerized workloads, monitoring, logging and operational support;
• Python and SQL (TypeScript is a plus), with the ability to support APIs, data workflows and platform integrations;
• Understanding of data engineering concepts: ETL, data pipelines, data storage and integration patterns;
• GenAI engineering tools such as GitHub Copilot, Cursor or OpenCode;
• Experience working in cross-functional, international teams;
• Pragmatic and outcome-driven, comfortable in an evolving AI environment;
• Fluent English;
• Snowflake, Azure AI Foundry, Microsoft Agent Framework, LangChain or MCP (highly valued);
• Frontend development, developer portals or internal platform interfaces (highly valued);
• Experience in multi-country enterprise environments (highly valued);
• Cloud certifications, DevSecOps, platform engineering or SRE practices (highly valued).
Ready to join us and succeed?
If you're tired of feeling like just a number, send us your application and become a Nimber!
